# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  FrenFlix configuration
#
#  Copy this file to `.env` and paste your Google OAuth client ID below — no
#  quotes, no spaces — then restart the dev server. Vite reads .env only at
#  startup.
#
#      Windows:  copy .env.example .env
#      macOS/Linux:  cp .env.example .env
#
#  Everything except the Drive panel works with this left empty: local files,
#  the player, the sync engine, subtitles, the queue. The Drive panel notices
#  it is unset and shows the setup steps instead of failing quietly.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Getting a client ID (about five minutes, once) ───────────────────────────
#
#   1. console.cloud.google.com → create or pick a project
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Google Drive API"
#   3. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → External, and add your own
#      Google account under "Test users"
#   4. Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application
#   5. Authorised JavaScript origins: add every origin you will use, exactly,
#      scheme included and no trailing slash. Google does not accept
#      wildcards:
#          http://localhost:5173
#          https://<your-project>.vercel.app
#   6. Paste the client ID above and restart
#
#  The scope requested is drive.readonly. Nothing in this app writes to Drive.
#  drive.readonly is a *restricted* scope, so an unverified app works only for
#  the accounts listed as Test users — up to 100 — which is what step 3 is for.
#  Without it, sign-in returns access_denied even when everything else is right.

# ── Two things that bite on deploy ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  1. `.env` IS GITIGNORED, SO IT WILL NOT REACH VERCEL.
#     Vite inlines VITE_* values into the bundle at build time, so the value
#     must exist *during the Vercel build*. Set it in the Vercel project
#     (Settings → Environment Variables) and redeploy. A value added after a
#     build is not in that build.
#
#  2. PREVIEW DEPLOYMENTS WILL FAIL SIGN-IN.
#     Each Vercel preview gets a fresh hostname, and Google has never seen it,
#     so you get origin_mismatch. Test Drive on the production domain, which
#     is stable. See DEPLOY.md.
#
#  A Google client ID is not a secret — it ships inside the JavaScript bundle
#  by design. What protects the account is the origin allow-list above.
